# Job: java framework/binding — ClientServer request reply is delivered to the caller only when its 5 s timeout fires (SupportChat sample fails after rebuild15)

You are a sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Cap 2.5 h. Read `AGENTS.md` §2/§3/§4.1/§5, `framework/AGENTS.md`. Campaign rules: no mitigations (no longer timeouts, retries, sleeps, polling), one owner per rule, root cause with a deterministic regression, public API unchanged. You MAY edit `bindings/java/**` and `framework/languages/java/**` (report which); never `core/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/**`, other languages. Do not commit. Locks: `/tmp/zlink-java-gate.lock` for gradle, `/tmp/zlink-samples-gate.lock` for samples. Check `/proc/loadavg` < 10.

## Symptom (framework gate g15, Core `602861c38b…` = main `2776ebb863`, packages rebuilt at 20:31)
`framework/languages/java/samples/run_samples.sh` → SupportChat fails; the other six java samples and all seven kotlin samples passed earlier today; cpp/dotnet/node SupportChat pass on the same Core. Log: `zlink-work/gates/g15/java-samples.log`.
- session node (PID 74440) sends ClientServer request `AuthenticateUserReq` to the api node at 20:46:41.642 (`phase=sent`).
- api node (74439) `received 41.646 → admitted → dispatched → replied 41.677` (35 ms).
- session node logs `phase=reply_received outcome=succeeded` for that request at **20:46:46.594 on thread `[channel-timeout]`** — i.e. the reply becomes visible to the framework exactly when the 5 s timeout task runs (`ZLinkChannelCallRuntime.track` schedules only `result.completeExceptionally(DEADLINE_EXCEEDED)` on `timeoutExecutor`).
- consequently `EnsureSupportUserActorReq` fails (`reply_received outcome=failed` on `[send-completion]`), the STREAM `AuthenticateReq` handler throws (`dispatch_error reason=handler_exception action=reply_error`), and the client's request times out after PT5S.
The java binding's request path: framework `ZLinkChannelDirectCalls.request` → `runtime.requestClient(target, parts, remaining)` → binding `dealer.request(...)`; completions are drained by the binding's per-context `CompletionPump` (`drainFromRuntime`, settlements=null) and settled through `Pending.captureRequest`/`publishRequest` (`bindings/java/.../CompletionOwner.java:990-1070`).

## What changed today (suspects, in order)
1. bindings/java R3 commits `4f73f6cd8d`, `9475357b23`, `59c03e6255`, `e292161adc`, `9ead6da9de` (blocking SEND/reply no longer hold the drain lock; shared native read guard), `a4f8cde0ef` (WRITABLE retries after NO_DATA) — the binding suite (115 unit, 25 integration, samples 7/7) passed, but the framework uses the runtime pump owner without a public poller.
2. Core: `973ebe30d5` (STREAM single-part, disconnect progress), `1b8816a72f` (D-118 hold-release credit waiter), `8c691f6c7a` (D-137: PEER_WEIGHT_CHANGED now emitted at admission/reconnect — previously silent), `9d6d84f3c6` (D-138 disconnect drains queued commands; STREAM first pipe after connect). Java may handle the newly emitted weight event on the ClientServer client (`ZLinkChannelSocketRegistry` / `ZLinkClientServerLocationRuntime`) in a way that stalls or re-registers the outbound.
3. framework/java today: `5a94c719ee` (ClientServer readiness snapshot + outbound classification via registry), `ac5b6a6b92` (relocation state machine), `a77f12168a`, `79094d9f1f` (clock seam).

